WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.439
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.439 --> 00:00:09.230
This is an episode that doesn't have the usual
visual fireworks and is expected to get fewer

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.280
clicks, but it is an important story to tell,
and because of your support, we are able to

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.030
cover a paper like this.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:23.880
So now, get this, this is a non-invasive brain-to-brain
interface that uses EEG to record brain signals

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.960
and TMS to deliver information to the brain.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.230
The non-invasive part is quite important,
it basically means that we don't need to drill

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.420
a hole in the head of the patients.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.550
That's a good idea.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:40.300
This image shows three humans connected via
computers, 2 senders and one receiver.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.260
The senders provide information to the receiver
about something he would otherwise not know

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:50.749
about, and we measure if they are able to
collaboratively solve a problem together.

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:55.500
These people never met each other, and don't
even know each other, and they can collaborate

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.359
through this technique directly via brain
signals.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.569
Wow!

00:01:00.569 --> 00:01:06.130
The BCI means brain-computer interface, and
the CBI, as you guessed, the computer-brain

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.189
interface.

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:12.729
So these brain signals can be encoded and
decoded and freely transferred between people

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:14.259
and computers.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:15.450
Insanity.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:19.850
After gathering all this information, the
receiver makes a decision, which the senders

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.930
also have access to, and can transmit some
more information if necessary.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.180
So what do they use it for?

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.320
Of course, to play Tetris!

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:33.979
Jokes aside, this is a great experiment where
the goal is to clear a line.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:35.859
Simple enough, right?

00:01:35.859 --> 00:01:38.020
Not so much, because there is a twist.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.859
The receiver only sees what you see here on
the left side.

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:46.220
This is the current piece we have to place
on the field, but the receiver has no idea

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:50.030
how to rotate it because he doesn't see its
surroundings.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:55.110
But the senders do, so they transmit the appropriate
information to the receiver who will now be

00:01:55.110 --> 00:02:02.390
able to make an informed decision as to how
to rotate the piece correctly to clear a line.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.569
So, does it work?

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:09.940
The experiment is designed in a way that there
is a 50% chance to be right without any additional

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.020
information for the receiver, so this will
be the baseline result.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:21.971
And the results are between 75% and 85%, which
means that the interface is working, and the

00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:25.330
brain-to-brain collaboration is now a reality.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.360
I am out of words.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.080
The paper also talks about brain-to-brain
social networks, and all kinds of science

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.390
fiction like that.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:39.030
My head is about to explode with the possibilities,
who knows, maybe in a few years, we can make

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:44.730
a superintelligent brain that combines all
of our expertise and does research for all

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:45.730
of us.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.390
Or, writes Two Minute Papers episodes.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.980
This paper is a must read.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.910
Do you have any other ideas as to how this
could enhance our lives?

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.540
Let me know below in the comments.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.400
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

